ACL (Android Compatibility Layer)

ACL's own source is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

A release bundle redistributes third-party components under their own terms.

Android Open Source Project — Apache License 2.0
    The managed runtime under art/ (libart and the boot class path jars), the
    resource and asset machinery, and the arm64 native bridge stubs are taken
    from AOSP. The full text of the Apache License 2.0 is at
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 and the per-file licence
    headers are kept intact in the sources under third_party/.

    android/android.jar is the Android SDK platform archive, redistributed for
    its framework resource table.

LLVM — Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
    lib/libLLVM.so and lib/liblld*.so, plus bin/ld.lld, come from the LLVM
    project. See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt.

Roboto — Apache License 2.0
    The fonts under fonts/ are from the Roboto project.

Other libraries under lib/
    FreeType (FTL or GPLv2), HarfBuzz (MIT), libpng (PNG Reference Library
    License), libjpeg-turbo (BSD-3-Clause and IJG), libwebp (BSD-3-Clause),
    SQLite (public domain), zlib (zlib licence), zstd (BSD-3-Clause and
    GPLv2), xz/liblzma (public domain and others), libxml2 (MIT), Wayland
    (MIT), libxkbcommon (MIT), PipeWire (MIT), GLib (LGPL-2.1-or-later),
    brotli (MIT), graphite2 (LGPL-2.1-or-later or MPL-1.1), libffi (MIT),
    libedit (BSD-3-Clause), ncurses/libtinfo (MIT), PCRE2 (BSD-3-Clause),
    bzip2 (BSD-4-Clause-like).

    These are copied from the build host unmodified. Their licence texts ship
    with the distributions they came from; see docs/provenance.md for how each
    one entered the tree.
